  "scientific_interpretation": {
    "tradeoff_observed": true,
    "summary": "Lowering the LGG classification threshold (tau_lgg from 0.50 down to 0.40-0.35) substantially increases LGG recall (from 41.67% up to 66.67%-83.33%) while causing only a modest reduction in HGG recall (from 97.16% down to 94.89%-90.91%). This confirms an empirical threshold-dependent operating-point trade-off without asserting a full causal resolution of the minority class learning dynamics."
